WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.460
In this video, you create a Longhorn storage class with a single replica. Storage classes decide how new volumes are provisioned, so a one-node cluster needs one that fits.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:17.770
The Storage Classes page, under Advanced, lists every class with its provisioner and number of replicas.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.190
Select Create.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.800
Give the storage class a name.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.680
Keep the Longhorn V1 provisioner, the default.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:33.930
Set the number of replicas to one. With a single node, Longhorn has nowhere to place a second copy.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.130
Keep the other parameters at their defaults.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.590
Select Create.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:44.090
The new storage class appears in the list with one replica.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:52.470
When you create a volume, the new storage class is now one of the choices.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:59.730
The storage class is ready. Volumes and virtual machine disks can now use it. Next, you set up cluster networking.
